From: Harunobu Kurokawa <harunobu.kurokawa.dn@renesas.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] spa/libcamera: fix build against libcamera's Model
 string_view control

libcamera's properties::Model control is declared as
Control<std::string_view> (see property_ids.h), not Control<std::string>.
std::string's constructor from std::string_view is explicit in C++17, so
returning std::move(model.value()) from a function that returns
std::string fails to compile:

  error: could not convert '...' from 'std::basic_string_view<char>' to
  'std::string'

Use an explicit std::string conversion instead. This plugin isn't
normally built (PACKAGECONFIG[libcamera] is opt-in), so this gap wasn't
caught upstream; needed here now that AGL enables it for boards that
advertise MACHINE_FEATURES += " libcamera".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp
index 210351c75..9042c0a57 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp
+++ b/spa/plugins/libcamera/libcamera-device.cpp
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@ static std::string cameraModel(const Camera *camera)
 	const ControlList &props = camera->properties();

 	if (auto model = props.get(properties::Model))
-		return std::move(model.value());
+		return std::string(model.value());

 	return camera->id();
 }
